Build the library for wasm32-wasip1: mimalloc only on non-wasm targets

mimalloc is the CLI's global allocator (main.rs) and does not build for
wasm32-wasip1; the library does not use it. It becomes a non-wasm target
dependency and the #[global_allocator] is cfg'd to non-wasm, so native
builds are unchanged.
Upstream: none (no related issue or PR; open issues #3 and #5 are
soundness reports, checked 2026-11-22).

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 7a81bf7..a8ce1fa 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -19,6 +19,9 @@ path = "src/main.rs"
 serde_json = "1"
 rustc-hash = "2"
 num-bigint = "0.5.1"
+
+# Only the CLI's global allocator; mimalloc does not build for wasm32-wasip1.
+[target.'cfg(not(target_family = "wasm"))'.dependencies]
 mimalloc = "0.1"
 
 [lints.rust]
diff --git a/src/main.rs b/src/main.rs
index 9dfc58d..7b19fd2 100644
--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+#[cfg(not(target_family = "wasm"))]
 #[global_allocator]
 static GLOBAL: mimalloc::MiMalloc = mimalloc::MiMalloc;
 
